      "commonError": "Treating spending and income as unrelated totals instead of two sides of the same transaction.",
      "q": "A firm produces $600,000 of final output. It pays $350,000 in wages, $100,000 in rent, $50,000 in interest, and keeps $100,000 in profit. What does this example show about GDP measurement?",
      "options": [
        "Expenditure on output and income earned from production both equal $600,000",
        "Only wages count in GDP, so GDP is $350,000",
        "Profit is excluded from GDP, so GDP is $500,000",
        "GDP cannot be measured from income"
      ],
      "tag": "gdp_income_expenditure",
      "type": "multi-step",
      "objective": "LO24.1",
      "feedback": "The value of final output equals the income generated in producing it: wages, rent, interest, and profit all add to $600,000.",
