      "commonError": "Confuses normal job search with skill mismatch or recession layoffs.",
      "feedback": "More generous benefits can lengthen search by reducing urgency, putting upward pressure on frictional unemployment. Faster and better referrals shorten matching time, putting downward pressure on it. Without their relative magnitudes the net effect is ambiguous.",
      "aHash": "1b0581a7746eb3f5116cafc65f514b160c60c30b2533eb4982d65f495487a335",
      "canonicalId": "PM2B4-LMI-H-001",
