      "commonError": "Incorrectly concludes “Both observations imply cyclical unemployment rose because matching institutions affect only demand” in this labor market institutions task.",
      "q": "A benefit reform gives 220 unemployed workers more time to search for good matches. Search duration rises, while later job retention also improves. Which policy assessment recognizes the tradeoff?",
