      "commonError": "Incorrectly concludes “Real GDP falls 20%; lower prices reduce real output at any nominal spending” in this real versus nominal gdp task.",
      "q": "An economy reports nominal GDP $1560 and real GDP $1300. Next year nominal GDP remains $1560 while its deflator falls from 120 to 100. Which inference is valid?",
