      "commonError": "Incorrectly concludes “The benefit rises 4% and real purchasing power rises 2% because inflation is subtracted in the opposite direction” in this indexing and real values task.",
      "q": "A $140 benefit rises by the previous year's 4% CPI increase. This year both CPI and the recipient's own living costs rise 6%. An official blames the real loss on a mismatch between the CPI basket and the recipient's purchases. Does that explanation fit?",
