      "repairSkill": "real_gdp_per_person",
      "commonError": "Incorrectly concludes “The one-time gain permanently doubles the growth rate by arithmetic identity” in this living standards and growth task.",
      "q": "A country with initial real GDP per person $140 sustains 4% growth instead of 2%. Another policy raises the level once by 4% but leaves later growth at 2%. Which comparison recognizes the long-run distinction?",
