      "id": "ERQ-PM2B2-DEF-LB-001",
      "q": "A country initially produces $200 of export machinery and households buy only imported food. Machinery prices fall 4% and food prices rise 6%, with quantities fixed. An analyst deflates the new nominal GDP using the food-price increase and reports a real contraction. Is that result sound?",
