      "commonError": "Incorrectly concludes “Real growth is 20%; the change in the price vector determines real output” in this real versus nominal gdp task.",
      "feedback": "With uniform quantity growth, the whole fixed-price sum is multiplied by 1.10 regardless of the chosen positive weights. Nominal growth is 1.10×1.20−1=32%. This weight-invariance depends on uniform quantity growth; it is not a general rule for changing output composition.",
